<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amuktamalyada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Amuktamalyada is a Telugu epic poem composed by the Vijayanagara emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> in the early sixteenth century. It tells the story of the Tamil saint Andal, devoted to the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a>, and her marriage to the god, and includes a section of advice on statecraft and kingship. It is counted among the five great poems of Telugu literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amuktamalyada.jpg" alt="Amuktamalyada" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chavakiran at Telugu Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vijayanagara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
